Inside the covered timber footbridge, Léa — a stocky toddler about four heads tall with loose chin-length straight brown hair and bangs at her eyebrows, large brown eyes, and soft rounded features — stands on the wet dark wooden floorboards, facing right in her red wool knit cardigan over a white long-sleeve T-shirt, grey corduroy trousers, and brown leather ankle boots, her fingers firmly grasping the sleeve of Henri's coat as she looks straight up into his face. Henri — a slim elderly man with stooped posture, short combed gray wavy hair, brown eyes, and a full gray beard — stands beside her facing left in his long grey wool overcoat, bright orange knitted wool scarf, blue checked shirt, brown corduroy trousers, and black leather shoes, looking down at her with a gentle, level expression and calm brows, his hands resting easily at his sides. Flat on the dark timber boards between their feet, stretching away from the foot of a timber post, lies l'ombre — a flat, solid near-black shadow silhouette with long thin limbs, a smooth rounded head without features, perfectly matching Léa's posture. Overhead, the heavy dark timber trusses and diagonal roof braces frame the walkway, where a scattering of damp autumn leaves clings to the floorboards, and through the narrow slatted timber walls, the warm tones of autumn riverbanks show in the dim dusk light. In the background toward the far timber-framed exit, a distant passer-by in a long dark coat walks away along the bridge. Medium shot capturing the two figures from the waist down to the floorboards.

---METADATA---
