Along the riverside pavement beside the Landvogteischloss, all five members of the family stand together in a row facing the camera under clear autumn skies. On the left, Henri, a slim elderly man with stooped posture, gray wavy hair, and a full beard, wears his long grey wool overcoat, orange knit scarf, brown corduroy trousers, and black leather shoes, smiling warmly. Beside him, Élodie, an average-build young woman with loose mid-back light brown wavy hair and a silver necklace, wears her yellow chunky turtleneck sweater, long black skirt, black tights, and black ankle boots. In the centre, Léa, a stocky toddler with straight chin-length brown hair and bangs, beams in her red knit cardigan, white shirt, grey corduroy trousers, and brown boots. Next to her, Jules, a slim kindergarten boy with short combed dark brown hair, stands in his green hooded fleece jacket, grey T-shirt, blue jeans, and black trainers with white soles. On the right, Marc, an average-build young adult man with dark wavy hair, wears his brown waxed field jacket, white henley, dark blue jeans, and brown leather lace-up boots, looking ahead with a relaxed grin. Behind them, the stepped-gable stone castle and its round turret rise into the sky, flanked by autumn trees and the brown-tiled roof of the covered wooden bridge spanning the river. Wide shot showing all five figures from head to toe, leaving the bottom area open for text.

---METADATA---
